---
# After closing and draining, nothing is enabled; that's the intended end.
deadlock_detection: false
---

# Example 17-02: Cardinality counter liveness
# Messages are sent until the channel closes; every message is eventually
# acked. Liveness: after closing, pending eventually drains to zero.
# Demonstrates: liveness with cardinality counters
#
# Ack can turn MANY into MANY again, so the abstract graph has a loop where
# Ack runs forever and pending stays MANY. No real count can shrink forever,
# and the liveness engine ignores loops that decrement a counter without
# ever incrementing it. Send is unfair: sending may stop at any time.

action Init:
    pending = cardinality.counter(0)
    closing = False

atomic action Send:
    require not closing
    pending = pending.inc()

atomic fair action Close:
    require not closing
    closing = True

atomic fair action Ack:
    require not pending.is_zero()
    pending = oneof pending.dec()

eventually always assertion Drained:
    return closing and pending.is_zero()
